  "interpretation": [
    "The frozen design had little probability of rejecting the primary null for a common interaction around |gamma_AH|=0.30-0.35, close to the observed paper-level magnitude.",
    "Detection exceeded 80% at about |gamma_AH|=0.498 and 90% at about 0.539.",
    "The non-confirmatory primary result therefore does not establish absence of a moderate common interaction; it does argue against interpreting a missed very large common interaction as the sole explanation.",
    "These thresholds are retrospective operating characteristics, not an equivalence bound or confidence interval."
